Material Things (Physical entities that exist in the real world)
Core Physical Assets:

Aircraft - The physical aircraft
Engine - Physical engine type/model
EngineInstance - Specific physical engine (with serial number)
EnginePart - Physical part types
partInstance - Specific physical part (with serial number)
CriticalParts - Physical critical components
LifeLimitedPart - Physical parts with life limits

Infrastructure:

Warehouse - Physical facility
StorageLocation - Physical location within warehouse

Organizations (Physical entities):

Carrier - Airline/operator organization
Supplier - Supplier organization
DesignatedServiceProvider - Service provider organization

Qualities, Functions, Roles
Qualities/States:

AOG (Aircraft on Ground) - Critical state/condition
timeUsed - Usage quality of a part

Functions:

ATA - Functional classification system

Roles:

PoCustomer - Customer role in purchasing
Region - Geographic role/classification
Country - Geographic classification
State - Geographic subdivision

Information Things (Data that describes, prescribes, or identifies)
Identifiers:

serialNumber - Identifies specific instances
materialDocNumber - Document identifier
lineItemNumber - Line item identifier

Descriptive Data:

quantity - Amount in movement
date - Temporal data
type - Classification data
debitCreditIndicator - Transaction type indicator

Prescriptive Data:

ServiceBulletin - Maintenance requirements
PartServiceBulletin - Part-specific requirements
WorkScope - Prescribed work to be done
WorkscopeDetail - Detailed work specifications

Transactional Records:

PurchaseOrder - Purchase transaction record
POLineItem - Purchase order details
SalesOrder - Sales transaction record
VbakPOs - SAP purchase order records
MsegPOs - SAP material document records

Inventory Records:

Inventory - General inventory data
SpareInventory - Spare parts inventory
CSAInventory - Customer service agreement inventory
OptimalPartAllocation - Allocation planning data
PartMRP - Material requirements planning data
Commits - Commitment records
SparesTransferOfAssets - Transfer records
LID - Location identification data

Processes (Things that happen)
Maintenance Processes:

ShopVisit - Maintenance event
ShopVisitGate - Shop visit milestone/phase
disassemblyAndTest - D&T process
EnginePartRepair - Repair process

Movement Processes:

PartMovement - Physical movement of parts

Ticket/Workflow Processes:

OpenEnginePartRepairTicket - Active repair workflow
ClosedEnginePartRepairTicket - Completed repair workflow
EnginePartRepairTickets - General repair tickets
EnginePartRepairSourced - Sourcing process for repairs

Time Periods

date properties on various objects capture when things happen
Shop visit dates
Part movement dates
Ticket open/close dates
